# Rust
/target
**/*.rs.bk
*.pdb

# Cargo lock for libraries (kept in repo for the binary; libraries excluded)
# We keep Cargo.lock at the workspace root because torrentd ships a binary.

# Editor
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Generated bindings / build artifacts
**/bindings.rs
**/*.bc
**/build/

# Resume data / runtime artifacts
*.resume
*.resume.tmp
profile_assignments.json
# The pre-profiles names, kept deliberately. A daemon that read one of these
# leaves it on disk rather than deleting it — the assignment registry stays
# intact so a rollback has something to go back to, and the orphaned session
# state is the operator's to delete — so a tree that ran an older build still
# has them and must not start reporting them.
slot_assignments.json
session_state.dat
# Session state is per profile now: `session_state-<profile_id>.dat`.
session_state-*.dat
# Pool index (SQLite, WAL mode) — a `pool scan` against a repo-local config
# drops all four of these in the tree. `*.db` matches names *ending* in `.db`,
# so the copy the v3 migration takes aside needs its own pattern.
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
*.pre-v3.bak
*.pre-v3.bak.new

# Environment
.env
.env.local

# Coverage
*.profraw
*.profdata
/coverage

# mise — local, per-developer tool/env overrides (mise.toml is committed)
/.mise.local.toml
